@ ADD: asks for a name and a base32 secret, computes the midstates on the
@ calculator and appends the account to ACCTS.  -> 1 if added, else 0.
@ INPUT returns the raw text (INFORM would parse it as an object).
\<<
  IFERR
    "Account name:" { "" \Ga } INPUT
    "Base32 secret:" { "" \Ga } INPUT
    \-> n s
    \<<
      IF n SIZE NOT THEN "Empty name" DOERR END
      CLLCD "Computing..." 4 DISP
      n 1 12 SUB s B32D MIDS 2 \->LIST 1 \->LIST
      IF 'ACCTS' VTYPE -1 == THEN { } 'ACCTS' STO END
      ACCTS SWAP + 'ACCTS' STO
      1
    \>>
  THEN
    IF ERRM SIZE THEN ERRM MSGBOX END
    0
  END
\>>
